One row per feat. A feat = one spec = a short session chain of work. Keep each
feat small enough that a fresh session can carry it through requirements →
design → tasks → implementation. Columns (all required, matched by header name):

  #          display order
  Feat       kebab-case slug — becomes the spec directory name
  Objective  one line: the outcome this feat delivers
  Depends    comma-separated feat slugs that must be `done` first (— for none;
             range shorthand like `1-3` is a validation error — list slugs)
  Milestone  grouping label (e.g. M1); feats run in milestone then table order
  (P)        `P` if this feat MAY run in parallel with its milestone siblings
             (v1 honors the marker for ordering only)
  Refs       whitespace-separated [[wiki-page]], stack:<name>, and adr:<slug>
             tokens; each stack:<name> must match a docs/stack.md Decided row,
             each [[wiki-page]] a page under docs/wiki/pages/, and each
             adr:<slug> a decision record docs/adr/NNNN-<slug>.md (the why this
             feat depends on — inlined in full into its run brief)
-->

